After some debugging, I determined that

1. having a table to enumerate the options like getopt_long is good.
   - having a single table that enumerates all options is confusing
   - having subsequent APIs to, in effect, add information to options cumberson

1. managing complements and synonyms is confusing


After considering a number of alternatives, I have determined..

1. a three table approach is better
   - with two tables being optional

1. the single required table, provides the straightforward functionality
   of getopts_long
   - but allows us to add an infinite number of synonym

1. providing an explicit type (with other functionality) into a table that
   manages a "flag" variable (ala gitopt_long) allows 
   - cleanup descriptions
   - allows for initial and default values
   - better management of complements

As such, starting to refactor the scanop code under the new approach.
